WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.870
A French cartoonist picks up a pencil.

2
00:00:02.870 --> 00:00:06.130
Today's drawing will mock
a religion's beliefs.

3
00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:09.140
French law protects «la
liberté d'expression».

4
00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:11.820
The same law also sets limits.

5
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.930
A joke. «Un dessin de presse».

6
00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.380
A post on «les réseaux sociaux».

7
00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:19.280
Which side of the limit is each one on?

8
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:23.010
So where exactly is the line
between mocking a religion

9
00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.780
and insulting the people
who believe in it?

10
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.100
In this mission, you'll build Mission D1:

11
00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:32.530
one line, two zones, and cases to place.

12
00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.870
Then you'll look at the media today:

13
00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:40.120
newspapers, news online, and a
row over one TV channel's licence.

14
00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.200
Your mission: find exactly
where French law draws the line,

15
00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.210
and explain why it sits there.
